## Usage<a id="usage"></a>

Each section below covers one administration task: what its modules manage and
refuse, what you prepare and when to activate. It ends with the tasks of that
task's play and the names of its modules;
`ansible-doc {{ namespace }}.{{ collection_name }}.<module>`
shows a module's options, return values and own rules. Every example is the task
list of this play, run on the control node against an inventory host that
carries the endpoint's variables:

```yaml
---
- name: "Configure {{ product | default('Example Product') }}"
  hosts: "product_api"
  connection: "local"
  gather_facts: false
  become: false
  module_defaults:
    group/{{ namespace }}.{{ collection_name }}.api:
      url: "{% raw %}{{ product_url }}{% endraw %}"
      api_key: "{% raw %}{{ product_api_key }}{% endraw %}"
      api_secret: "{% raw %}{{ product_api_secret }}{% endraw %}"
  tasks: # the tasks of the section
```

